# The dashboard is a backend-for-frontend. It holds NO credential of its own (0198):
# it authenticates to the API as the signed-in operator, by forwarding their session
# cookie. There is no API key here to provision, rotate, or leak.
#
# TMBILLING_API_KEY used to live here, and it was not merely redundant — it, not the
# session, is what told the engine which ORGANIZATION to serve. An operator belonging
# to two organizations could switch, watch the whole UI change, and still be reading
# and writing the key's tenant.
#
# OPTIONAL — DEPRECATED AS THE PLACE FOR SETTINGS. Put these keys in the repository's root .env:
# the dashboard copies in only the keys in ROOT_ENV_KEYS (dashboard/root-env.mjs) and nothing else.
# A dashboard/.env.local still works and wins over the root file; the real environment wins over
# both. Keep one only to give this machine's dashboard a different value.
# TMBILLING_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Origin the API is reachable at from a BROWSER, or from a third party such as a payment
# gateway. TMBILLING_API_URL above is the server-to-server address this Next process dials
# the engine on, and in production that is typically a loopback port on the same box — so
# it must never be rendered into a link, a copyable field, or anything handed to a gateway.
#
# Set this to the same value the engine has as WEBHOOK_BASE_URL. Two screens depend on it:
# /developer (the /docs and openapi.json links) and a gateway account's Notification URL.
# When unset in a production build both DEGRADE rather than render an unreachable URL —
# the docs paths become plain text and the Notification URL is replaced by a warning.
# Unset in local dev is correct: there the two origins really are the same.
# TMBILLING_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.example.com

# API settings (root .env only — the dashboard never reads these two; they sit here for context):
# How long an invite link stays usable, in hours (0196). Longer than a password reset: a
# reset is something you asked for seconds ago; an invite arrives unannounced and may sit
# until someone is back at their desk. Needs DASHBOARD_BASE_URL, or no invite mail is
# composed at all (logged, never revealed to the inviter).
# INVITE_TTL_HOURS=72

# How long a hosted-checkout link stays usable, in hours (W10). Ours is a COPYABLE link an
# operator hands over — often by email — not one generated on a click from the merchant's
# own site, so it needs a longer life. 24h so a buyer sent a link this
# morning can still use it tonight, and nobody can use it next week. Deliberately REUSABLE
# unlike the portal link, which is single-use: abandoning a checkout and coming back is
# ordinary behaviour worth real money, and the link grants materially less.
# CHECKOUT_SESSION_TTL_HOURS=24

# Cloudflare Turnstile PUBLIC site key — the bot challenge on the forgot-password form
# (audit M3.2). The widget renders only when this is set, so an unconfigured deployment shows
# no challenge box rather than an unsolvable one.
#
# Pair it with TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY in the API's env. Set both or neither: a widget with no
# server-side check is decoration, and a server-side check with no widget is a form nobody can
# submit.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# Google sign-in PUBLIC values. Set them here and the sign-in page renders the Google button
# without asking the API first. They must equal the API's GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI exactly — the API exchanges the code with its own copies. Leave both
# unset to have the dashboard read them from the API's GET /auth/google instead.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:4100/auth/google/callback

# The edition, as the API's TMBILLING_EDITION: self_hosted (default) or cloud. Only cloud shows
# sign-up, the plan banners and Settings → Billing. Any other value refuses to build or start.
# TMBILLING_EDITION=self_hosted

# Account billing (Cloud only: needs TMBILLING_EDITION=cloud). Where the Billing page reads the
# organization's own plan, and the credential for it. Unset means no Billing page and no plan
# limits. ACCOUNT_BILLING_CONTACT_URL is the Enterprise "Contact us" link.
# ACCOUNT_BILLING_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4500
# ACCOUNT_BILLING_TOKEN=
# ACCOUNT_BILLING_CONTACT_URL=https://twominutebilling.com/contact
